{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro"},{"type":"text","text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s library declares the macro, the same kind, and the read of the set. It depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets and re-exports it, because the expansion calls LinkerSets’ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"text":" in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users’ files:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")","","extension Endpoints {","    public static var all: [Endpoint] {","        LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its users then register routes and read them through the library:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = Endpoints.all"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the re-export exposes","anchor":"What-the-re-export-exposes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Route static let home = ...","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" expands, in the user’s file, to one call:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Routes.home)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". That macro, which LinkerSets declares,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expands in turn to the record itself, one declaration per object format, naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So the user’s file has to see LinkerSets. With","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import LinkerSets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the client’s library, importing the client is enough. With a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain or ","type":"text"},{"code":"public import","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", every user’s file fails to compile with “no macro named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” until it imports LinkerSets itself. The compile tests in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tests\/CompileFailures","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"ExportingClientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ImportingClientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ImportingClientUserImportingLinkerSets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") check each case.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So every file that imports the client also sees "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" and anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"public the client adds to them. A kind constant doesn’t need to be public: the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"kind as a number, so users’ files never name the constant. Keep it internal and give users the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values through the client’s own API, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Endpoints.all"},{"type":"text","text":" does above. A user can still read the set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by its number, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)"},{"type":"text","text":"; an internal constant only keeps it out of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"autocomplete and out of the client’s public API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes the same record ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"text":" writes, in the same section, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'@Route' applies to static members only"},{"text":"). Each kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Registering types","anchor":"Registering-types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record then holds "},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Any.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Checking keys are unique","anchor":"Checking-keys-are-unique"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro can give each declaration a key that no other record of its kind in the same executable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or library may share, in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKey(of:attribute:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The expansion then adds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function whose symbol is named for the kind and the key, and a second declaration with the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key fails to compile in one module, or to link across modules:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func uniqueKey(of declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol, attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> String? {","        declaration.asProtocol(NamedDeclSyntax.self)?.name.text","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro whose users write the key returns "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKeyArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which reads a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey:"},{"type":"text","text":" string literal. An empty key, and a key on a member of a private type, are refused"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with diagnostics of their own. The check reaches one linked image only; LinkerSets’ guide to unique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys shows each linker’s message and the limits."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Declaring the kind once","anchor":"Declaring-the-kind-once"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin returns the kind from "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and the library reads the set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, so the number appears twice, and a mismatch shows only at run time, as an empty set. To write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it once, put it in a module of its own that depends on nothing, and have both import it:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ RoutesKind","public enum RouteKind {","    public static let rawValue: UInt32 = 0x726F_7574  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ RoutesMacros, the plugin","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { RouteKind.rawValue }","}"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Routes, the library","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: RouteKind.rawValue)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The package lists the module among both targets’ dependencies:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".macro(name: \"RoutesMacros\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", ...])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".target(name: \"Routes\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", \"RoutesMacros\", ...])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". SwiftPM builds it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the host for the plugin and for the target for the library.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Writing records without depending on LinkerSets","anchor":"Writing-records-without-depending-on-LinkerSets"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A module that uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" depends on LinkerSets, which builds LinkerSets’ own plugin,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetsMacros, and swift-syntax with it. A module that only writes a few records, such as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events of one feature, can skip that. A client with a plugin of its own declares two macros there:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an entry macro that takes the kind as an argument, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does, and a record macro","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its own under a different name, which the entry macro’s expansion calls in place of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ DiscoveryMacros, the plugin","@main","struct DiscoveryMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [DiscoverableMacro.self, DiscoverableRecordMacro.self]","}","","public enum DiscoverableMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) throws -> UInt32 {","        try kindArgument(of: attribute)","    }","","    public static var recordMacroName: String { \"discoverableRecord\" }","}","","public enum DiscoverableRecordMacro: DeclarationMacro {","    public static func expansion(","        of node: some FreestandingMacroExpansionSyntax,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try LinkerSetRecordMacro.expansion(of: node, in: context)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares both and re-exports LinkerSetsRuntime, whose names the record uses:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Discovery, the library","@_exported import LinkerSetsRuntime","","@attached(peer)","public macro Discoverable(kind: UInt32) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableMacro\")","","@freestanding(declaration)","public macro discoverableRecord<Value>(kind: UInt32, storing value: Value) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableRecordMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that writes records then depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Discovery"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime"},{"type":"text","text":", not on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets, and writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Discoverable(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"type":"text","text":" where it would have written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x7365_7373)"},{"type":"text","text":". Its build holds the client’s plugin, which already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs swift-syntax, and not LinkerSetsMacros. The record macro’s name must differ from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", because a module that imports both LinkerSets and the client couldn’t choose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between two macros of the same name."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Testing the expansion","anchor":"Testing-the-expansion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A client’s expansion tests pin one line per record, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["assertMacroExpansion(","    \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        @Route","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","    }","    \"\"\",","    expandedSource: \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","","        #linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Endpoints.home)","    }","    \"\"\",","    macroSpecs: [\"Route\": MacroSpec(type: RouteMacro.self)],","    failureHandler: { Issue.record(\"\\($0.message)\") }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertMacroExpansion"},{"type":"text","text":" expands only the macros in its table, so the call stays as written, and it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads the same on every swift-syntax from 600 on. The record behind it, one declaration per object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, belongs to LinkerSets and changes when LinkerSets adds a format. A test that wants it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyway adds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"linkerSetRecord\": MacroSpec(type: LinkerSetRecordMacro.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" to the table. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration at file scope expands to the call inside a private enum of its own, whose name comes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the context’s unique names ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"__macro_local_15linkerSetRecordfMu_"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Writing the expansion yourself","anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},{"text":" supplies the peer ","type":"text"},{"code":"expansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"text":" from it for the record. That’s how","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event struct Login {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds only its metatype, read as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" first. It returns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" says why, and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node"},{"type":"text","text":" is where to report it, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the declaration can hold a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other refusal still reaches "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the expansion."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their own.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Declaring a macro","anchor":"Declaring-a-macro","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetRecordMacro"]},{"title":"Diagnostics","anchor":"Diagnostics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":